# 1. Amendment Scope

This document is a full replacement of UX and UI Specification v1.3. All content from v1.3 remains in force. The sections below describe only the changes made in v1.4.

# 2. Section 7.2 — Report List Page Updates

The Report List page (Section 7.2) is updated as follows. All existing content in v1.3 Section 7.2 remains in force; the following is additive.

## 2.1 Draft Badge — Report List Card

| **Decision**** Report type cards displayed in the Report List for Report Developer and Administrator users include a status badge. Published report types show no badge — the absence of a badge signals published status. Draft report types display a MUI Chip with label ****'****Draft****'**** and colour=****'****warning****'**** (amber). The badge is positioned in the top-right corner of the report card. Standard users (non-Report Developer, non-Administrator) never see draft reports — they see only published reports, so they never see the Draft badge.** |
| --- |

| **Claude Code Note**** Report List card — status badge implementation:   Conditionally render ****<****Chip label=****'****Draft****'**** color=****'****warning****'**** size=****'****small****'**** /****>****   in the card header only when: (is_report_developer ││ is_administrator) ****&****&**** report.status === ****'****Draft****'****   Standard users receive only Published records from GET /api/v1/report-definitions,   so no conditional logic is needed for their card rendering.** |
