# 3. Section 7.6 — New: Report Definition Authoring

## 3.1 Overview

The report definition authoring surface allows Report Developers and Administrators to create, edit, publish, unpublish, and delete report types. It is accessible only to users with is_report_developer = TRUE or is_administrator = TRUE. The authoring surface consists of two screens: the Report Definition Management screen (the list of all report definitions) and the Report Definition Editor screen (the form for creating or editing a single report definition).

## 3.2 Report Definition Management Screen

### 3.2.1 Layout

The Report Definition Management screen is the landing page for the authoring surface. It is reached from 'Manage Reports' on the Report List page. Page header: breadcrumb 'Reporting > Manage Reports'; primary action button: 'New Report' (MUI Button, variant='contained').

The screen body displays all report definitions (Draft and Published) as a MUI Data Grid with the following columns:

| **Column** | **Source** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Report Name | report_name | Clickable link — navigates to the Report Definition Editor screen for that report. |
| Status | status | Rendered as a MUI Chip: 'Published' (color='success', green); 'Draft' (color='warning', amber). |
| Created By | created_by (resolved to display_name) | Display name of the creating user. |
| Created | created_at | Formatted as DD MMM YYYY. |
| Published | published_at | Formatted as DD MMM YYYY. Blank for Draft reports. |
| Columns | available_columns.length | Count of available columns defined in the report. |
| Actions | — | Row-level action menu (MUI IconButton with MoreVert icon). Actions: Edit (always), Publish (Draft only), Unpublish (Published only), Delete (Draft only — Published requires unpublish first). |

Default sort: created_at descending (most recent first). User may sort by any column. No pagination required — the total number of report definitions is expected to be small (< 50).

### 3.2.2 Empty State

When no report definitions exist: display a centred empty state — 'No reports have been created yet. Click New Report to create the first report definition.' with a 'New Report' MUI Button (variant='contained') below the message.

| **Claude Code Note**** Report Definition Management screen — route: /reporting/manage Component: src/components/reporting/ReportDefinitionManagement.tsx On load: GET /api/v1/report-definitions (authoring users receive all records — Draft and Published). Grid: MUI X Data Grid, no inline editing — all edits via the Editor screen. Row click on report name: navigate(****'****/reporting/manage/{report_id}****'****). New Report button: navigate(****'****/reporting/manage/new****'****).** |
| --- |

## 3.3 Report Definition Editor Screen

### 3.3.1 Layout

The Report Definition Editor is a full-page form. It is used for both creating new report definitions and editing existing ones. Page header: breadcrumb 'Reporting > Manage Reports > [Report Name or New Report]'. Primary action buttons in the page header bar:

- Save — saves the current form state as a Draft (creates or updates). Enabled when the form is dirty and valid. Disabled when the form is clean or invalid.

- Publish — transitions status to Published. Enabled only when status = 'Draft' and the form is clean (saved). Disabled on unsaved Draft or on Published reports.

- Unpublish — transitions status to Draft. Enabled only when status = 'Published'. Disabled on Draft reports.

- Delete — deletes the report definition. Enabled only when status = 'Draft'. Disabled on Published reports (must unpublish first). Uses destructive (error) button colour.

The form body is a single scrollable column with two sections: Report Details (top) and Column Configuration (below).

### 3.3.2 Report Details Section

The Report Details section contains:

- Report Name — MUI TextField, required, maximum 100 characters, character counter displayed below field. Validation: non-empty, unique across all report definitions (validated server-side on Save — HTTP 409 if duplicate). Inline error message below field on validation failure.

- Description — MUI TextField, multiline (3 rows), optional, maximum 500 characters, character counter displayed below field.

- Status indicator — read-only MUI Chip showing current status (Draft / Published). Not editable directly — changed via Publish/Unpublish actions.

### 3.3.3 Column Configuration Section

### 3.3.3.1 Section Layout

The Column Configuration section has a two-panel layout: an Available Columns panel on the left (all reportable fields not yet added to this report) and a Report Columns panel on the right (columns added to this report definition). A divider separates the panels. Each panel has a heading and a scrollable list.

| **Decision**** Available Columns panel — left, ~40% width. Displays all reportable fields defined in Reporting FR v1.0 Sections 7 and 8 that have not been added to the current report. Each row shows the field display name and data type. A search/filter input at the top of the panel allows filtering by name. Report Columns panel — right, ~60% width. Displays the columns selected for this report definition. Each row shows: drag handle (for reordering), column display name, Default Visible toggle (MUI Switch), is_compensation indicator (lock icon for compensation fields), and a Remove button (MUI IconButton, delete icon).** |
| --- |

### 3.3.3.2 Adding Columns

Columns are added from the Available Columns panel to the Report Columns panel by clicking the column row or by clicking an 'Add' icon button on the right of each available column row. On add, the column moves from Available to Report Columns, appended at the bottom of the Report Columns list. The Available Columns panel updates immediately to exclude the added column.

### 3.3.3.3 Removing Columns

Columns are removed from the Report Columns panel via the Remove icon button on each row. On remove, the column returns to the Available Columns panel. At least one column must remain in the Report Columns panel — the Remove button is disabled when only one column remains. Inline validation message: 'At least one column is required.'

### 3.3.3.4 Reordering Columns

Columns in the Report Columns panel may be reordered via drag-and-drop (MUI X Data Grid row reordering or a custom drag-handle implementation). The order in the Report Columns panel determines the left-to-right column order in the report viewer for users who have not customised their column order.

### 3.3.3.5 Default Visibility Toggle

Each column in the Report Columns panel has a Default Visible toggle (MUI Switch). When enabled (TRUE), the column is visible by default when a user first opens the report. When disabled (FALSE), the column is hidden by default and must be explicitly enabled by the user via the column visibility panel in the report viewer. At least one column must have default_visible = TRUE — inline validation message shown if all toggles are set to FALSE: 'At least one column must be visible by default.'

| **Claude Code Note**** Column configuration — implementation: Component: src/components/reporting/ColumnConfigurator.tsx State: two arrays — availableColumns (not in report) and reportColumns (in report, ordered). Initialise on load:   availableColumns = all reportable fields (from a static config or API) MINUS those in report.available_columns.   reportColumns = report.available_columns (ordered array from the stored JSON). On Add: move item from availableColumns to end of reportColumns. On Remove: move item from reportColumns back to availableColumns (sorted by display_name). On Reorder: update reportColumns array order via drag result. On Default Visible toggle: update reportColumns[i].default_visible boolean. Persist: serialize reportColumns array to JSON and include in PATCH body as available_columns. Drag-and-drop: use @hello-pangea/dnd (fork of react-beautiful-dnd) for row reordering.   Wrap Report Columns list in ****<****DragDropContext****>****, ****<****Droppable****>****, and ****<****Draggable****>****. Search/filter in Available Columns: client-side filter on display_name (case-insensitive contains).** |
| --- |

## 3.4 Save Behaviour

The Save button in the page header submits the current form state:

- New report: POST /api/v1/report-definitions — creates a new Draft record. On success: navigate to the editor URL for the new report_id; show success toast: 'Report saved.'

- Existing report: PATCH /api/v1/report-definitions/{id} — updates name, description, available_columns. On success: clear dirty state; show success toast: 'Report saved.'

- Validation errors: inline field-level messages. API validation errors (e.g., duplicate name — HTTP 409) are shown as an inline error banner below the Report Name field: 'A report with this name already exists.'

- Save is disabled when the form has no changes (clean state) or when required fields are empty.

## 3.5 Publish Flow

The Publish button is available only when status = 'Draft' and the form is in a clean (saved) state. If the form is dirty, the user must Save before publishing.

- Clicking Publish opens a confirmation modal: title 'Publish report'; body 'Publishing [Report Name] will make it visible to all users in the Report List. Are you sure?' Actions: 'Publish' (primary) | 'Cancel'.

- On confirmation: PATCH /api/v1/report-definitions/{id} with { status: 'Published' }. On success: status chip updates to Published; Publish button disables; Unpublish button enables; success toast: 'Report published. It is now visible in the Report List.'

- Publish is blocked if no columns are configured — inline validation message shown.

## 3.6 Unpublish Flow

The Unpublish button is available only when status = 'Published'.

- Clicking Unpublish opens a confirmation modal: title 'Unpublish report'; body 'Unpublishing [Report Name] will hide it from the Report List. Users with saved filters for this report will not be able to apply them until it is re-published. Are you sure?' Actions: 'Unpublish' (primary) | 'Cancel'.

- On confirmation: PATCH /api/v1/report-definitions/{id} with { status: 'Draft' }. On success: status chip updates to Draft; Unpublish button disables; Publish button enables; success toast: 'Report unpublished. It is no longer visible in the Report List.'

## 3.7 Delete Flow

The Delete button is available only when status = 'Draft'. Published reports cannot be deleted — the Delete button is disabled with tooltip: 'Unpublish this report before deleting.'

- Clicking Delete opens a confirmation modal: title 'Delete report'; body 'Deleting [Report Name] is permanent and cannot be undone.' Actions: 'Delete' (primary, error/destructive colour) | 'Cancel'.

- On confirmation: DELETE /api/v1/report-definitions/{id}. On success: navigate to /reporting/manage; show success toast: 'Report deleted.'

## 3.8 Unsaved Change Warning

Navigating away from the Report Definition Editor with unsaved changes (dirty form) triggers the standard OBS unsaved change warning modal: title 'Unsaved changes'; actions 'Save and leave' | 'Leave without saving' | 'Cancel'. This follows the same pattern as the Budget Planning module (UX v1.3 Section 5.3.6).

## 3.9 Navigation and Access Control

- The /reporting/manage route and all sub-routes are accessible only to users with is_report_developer = TRUE or is_administrator = TRUE. Any other user navigating to these routes sees the standard HTTP 403 inline access denied message.

- The 'Manage Reports' button in the Report List page header and the 'New Report' button are not rendered for standard users — they are not shown in a disabled state.

| **Claude Code Note**** Report Definition Editor — route: /reporting/manage/new (create) and /reporting/manage/{id} (edit). Component: src/components/reporting/ReportDefinitionEditor.tsx On load (edit): GET /api/v1/report-definitions/{id}. Show CircularProgress while loading. Dirty state: track with React state — set to true on any form field change.   Clear dirty state on successful Save.   Prompt unsaved change modal on React Router navigation away if dirty === true. Publish button disabled conditions: status !== ****'****Draft****'**** OR dirty === true OR reportColumns.length === 0. Unpublish button disabled conditions: status !== ****'****Published****'****. Delete button disabled conditions: status !== ****'****Draft****'****.   If status === ****'****Published****'****: show Delete button with disabled=true and MUI Tooltip:     ****'****Unpublish this report before deleting.****'** |
| --- |

# 4. Acceptance Criteria — Report Definition Authoring

| **ID** | **Criterion** |
| --- | --- |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-01 | The 'Manage Reports' button is rendered in the Report List page header for users with is_report_developer = TRUE or is_administrator = TRUE. It is not rendered for any other user. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-02 | Draft report type cards in the Report List display a 'Draft' amber MUI Chip badge. Published report type cards display no status badge. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-03 | The Report Definition Management screen displays all report definitions (Draft and Published) in a sortable MUI Data Grid when accessed by an authorised user. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-04 | Clicking a report name in the management grid navigates to the Report Definition Editor for that report. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-05 | Clicking 'New Report' navigates to the Report Definition Editor in create mode (empty form). |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-06 | The Report Definition Editor displays two sections: Report Details (name, description, status) and Column Configuration (available columns and report columns panels). |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-07 | Adding a column from the Available Columns panel moves it to the Report Columns panel and removes it from Available Columns. The change is reflected immediately in the UI without a page reload. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-08 | Removing a column from the Report Columns panel returns it to the Available Columns panel. The Remove button is disabled when only one column remains in Report Columns. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-09 | Columns in the Report Columns panel can be reordered via drag-and-drop. The updated order is reflected in the saved available_columns JSON on Save. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-10 | Each column in the Report Columns panel has a Default Visible toggle. The toggle state is saved as the default_visible field in the available_columns JSON. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-11 | An inline validation message is displayed if all Default Visible toggles are set to FALSE: 'At least one column must be visible by default.' The Save button remains enabled — this is a warning, not a blocking error. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-12 | The Save button calls POST /api/v1/report-definitions for new reports and PATCH /api/v1/report-definitions/{id} for existing reports. On success, a 'Report saved.' success toast is shown and the dirty state is cleared. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-13 | A duplicate report name returns HTTP 409 from the API. The editor displays an inline error below the Report Name field: 'A report with this name already exists.' The form remains open. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-14 | The Publish button is disabled when the form is dirty or when status = 'Published'. Clicking Publish opens a confirmation modal. On confirmation, the report status transitions to Published and the status chip updates to green. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-15 | The Unpublish button is disabled when status = 'Draft'. Clicking Unpublish opens a confirmation modal. On confirmation, the report status transitions to Draft and the status chip updates to amber. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-16 | The Delete button is disabled when status = 'Published'. A tooltip reads 'Unpublish this report before deleting.' For Draft reports, clicking Delete opens a confirmation modal. On confirmation, the report is deleted and the user is navigated to /reporting/manage. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-17 | Navigating away from the editor with unsaved changes triggers the standard OBS unsaved change warning modal with 'Save and leave', 'Leave without saving', and 'Cancel' options. |
| AC-UP-RPT-AUTH-18 | Navigating directly to /reporting/manage or /reporting/manage/{id} as a non-Report Developer, non-Administrator user displays the standard HTTP 403 inline access denied message. |

